        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Andreas Dilger",
          "email": "adilger@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-11-13 07:17:25.000000000",
          "tz": -360
        },
        "subject": "LU-21103 lov: select the mirror of a read in one place",
        "message": "LU-21103 lov: select the mirror of a read in one place\n\nlov_io_mirror_init() decides which mirror an IO of a mirrored file\nuses in one loop that both judges each mirror and sets the cl_io and\nlov_io fields as it goes, then runs the retry backoff and the\nci_ndelay/ci_no_soft_tmo policy at a label that the CIT_EC_RD path\njumps to.  A change to which mirror a read prefers, such as avoiding\na slow-marked OST, has to be threaded through all of it.\n\nMove mirror selection to a new file lov_mirror.c and split it in\nthree.  lov_mirror_evaluate() says how one mirror can serve the IO,\nas a verdict, without changing the IO.  lov_io_select_mirror() tries\nthe mirrors in turn, acts on the verdicts and sets the IO fields,\nci_no_soft_tmo once for the mirror it picks.  lov_io_mirror_backoff()\nholds the backoff after each round of mirrors, which both the\nselection and the CIT_EC_RD path go through, replacing the\nndelay_retry label.  lov_io_mirror_init() keeps the CIT_EC_RD,\nnon-FLR, designated mirror and write intent paths.\nlov_has_parity_mirror() and lov_io_data_mirrors() move with it;\nlov_find_comp_with_ec(), lov_io_parity_eof() and\nlov_io_top_file_size() are no longer static.\n\nNo functional change.\n\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nSigned-off-by: Keguang Xu <kxu@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Augment Agent:Claude Opus 5.5\nChange-Id: Iab4f84525a20c568108e53cb97d85ed345d24cfe\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
